he language to understand the precise meaning of the question. The phrasing suggests I need to determine the proportion of accepted tenders from global non-domestic investors in relation to the total bids. The ambiguity lies in whether \"these\" refers to total bids or accepted tenders. However, the emphasis on \"tenders accepted\" points to using the $6,001 million figure as the denominator.\n\nCalculating the percentage using different denominators yields distinct results. Using $6,001 million gives 7.96%, while $10,102 million yields 4.73%. I'm leaning toward the interpretation that matches \"tenders accepted\" - using the total accepted tender amount as the base.\n\nThe specific wording \"noncash rollover tenders accepted submitted on the behalf of global non-domestic investors\" indicates the $478 million is the numerator. The key is confirming this represents noncash rollover tenders, which appear to be securities exchanged for maturing securities.\n\nI'm now considering whether \"these\" might actually refer to total accepted tenders, leading to a calculation of 7.96%. However, I'll verify the precise definition by carefully reviewing the context to ensure accuracy.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_300b8bda43f04223b6aafdb5","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Find data about 2-year U.S. Treasury notes maturing at end of July 1984\n- [x] Identify total dollar value of bids submitted by investors\n- [x] Identify percent of noncash rollover tenders accepted for global non-domestic investors\n- [x] Return answer as [total_dollar_value, percent_value] in comma-separated values"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
