as part of the $6,001 million total accepted.\n\n\nI'll calculate the precise percentage of accepted tenders from foreign investors. By dividing $478 million by $6,001 million and multiplying by 100, I get 7.96%. This matches my previous calculation and confirms the interpretation that we're looking at the proportion of accepted tenders from global non-domestic investors.\n\nI'm questioning the precise interpretation of \"these\" in the original question. The phrase could potentially refer to either total bids or accepted tenders, which introduces some ambiguity. However, the context suggests we're focusing on accepted tenders from international investors.\n\nI'll carefully verify the calculation to ensure accuracy in representing the percentage of noncash rollover tenders.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_89d6367a508d4db6813bdd07","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/answer.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
